('be7dd063-606d-58c0-8911-b50d62a13139', 'RBI/2019-20/67 Harmonisation of TAT', 'p.2', 2, '2019-09-20', 'https://www.rbi.org.in', '4. It may be noted that :  
 
• the prescribed TAT is the outer limit for resolution of failed transactions; 
and  
• the banks and other  operators / system participants shall endeavour 
towards quicker resolution of such failed transactions. 
 
5. Wherever financial compensation is involved, the same shall be effected to the 
customer’s account suo moto,  without waiting for a complaint or claim from the 
customer.  
 
6. Customers who do not get the benefit of redress of the failure as defined in the 
TAT, can regi ster a complaint with the Reserve Bank - Integrated Ombudsman 
Scheme, 2021 (as amended from time to time).  
 
7. This directive is issued under Section 10(2) read with Sect ion 18 of the 
Payment and Settlement Systems Act, 2007 (Act 51 of 2007) and shall come into 
effect from October 15, 2019.  
 
Yours faithfully 
 
 
(P. Vasudevan) 
Chief General Manager 
 
